# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Exported per-NTA drill-down data (tract/route/facility) -- the raw
# per-NTA route exports in routes/ (every sport x both time windows x every
# route option) run ~548MB total and are pipeline intermediate output, not
# something the frontend ever fetches directly -- stay ignored. tracts/ is
# only ~8MB total for all 262 NTAs, so it's committed in full. routes/ only
# un-ignores the pre-filtered soccer/weekday_evening slice per NTA (see
# scripts/extract_soccer_weekday_evening_routes.py) -- the only sport+window
# NtaRouteDetail.tsx currently renders. Originally un-ignored for just
# Elmhurst's (QN0401) worked example (per project owner instruction,
# 2026-10-06); widened to every NTA per project owner instruction,
# 2026-11-18, after a teammate found the committed route/tract data only
# covered Elmhurst.
/public/data/routes/*
!/public/data/routes/*_soccer_weekday_evening.geojson
/public/data/facilities/*
!/public/data/facilities/soccer.geojson
/public/data/nta_boundaries.geojson
